    "title": "New Cookbook Champions Seafood for All Meals",
    "text": "•\tAndrew Zimmern and Barton Seaver, in collaboration with Fed by Blue, have created \"The Blue Food Cookbook: Delicious Recipes for a Sustainable Future.\"\n•\tThe cookbook aims to make food from oceans, lakes, and rivers less confusing.\n•\t\"Blue food\" encompasses ocean and freshwater animals, algae, and marine plants.\n•\tThe authors argue that choosing blue food doesn't have to be difficult or expensive.\n•\tThe book addresses concerns about seafood sustainability and sourcing.\n•\tThe book includes 145 recipes, ranging from high-end to everyday dishes.\n•\tThe book provides cooking techniques, buying tips, and pantry essentials.\n•\tThe book features dueling recipes for certain dishes, showcasing different approaches.\n•\tThe authors advocate for seafood consumption at all meals, including breakfast.\n•\tThe book includes seafood breakfast ideas from various cultures.",
